WEBVTT

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:21.710
Fayora, it's not a good idea to advertise you from another planet.

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.710
You may feel more human than Kryptonian.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:25.710
This is who I am.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.710
Just when you're out in public, it's better to keep those tags hidden places.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:33.710
How can we be safe when someone destroyed our tower?

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:35.710
Could have been brought down by anyone.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:40.280
I don't even know who to trust anymore.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.280
I know how much that tower meant to you, to all of you, but you can't change what happens in the past.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.280
Zod told us it was our salvation.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.280
And he was wrong. Trust me, the future would be much bright.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.280
My future would be much brighter without it.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.280
Only one thing gives me hope.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.280
You found my sister and brought her back to me.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:03.670
This is Clark.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:06.670
Remember? You both need to call me by my human name.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:10.670
Clark, it just sounds so alien.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.670
I came by to check on you both.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.670
I understand how difficult it can be adjusting to a new home.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:18.670
Without our powers, adjusting will be even more difficult.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:21.670
Fayora, we have nothing to fear anymore.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:29.819
He'll protect us.

00:01:29.819 --> 00:01:30.819
They need you too.

00:01:30.819 --> 00:01:42.780
Sister, don't get your hopes up. He's in love with a human.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.780
Close up and meet me across the street.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:48.780
You can drown your sorrows in one of their cappuccinos.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:02:13.729
Sorry, we're closed.

00:02:13.729 --> 00:04:58.269
Hello? Juggling deadlines like I'm trying out for Cirque de Soleil.

00:04:58.269 --> 00:05:01.899
What about you?

00:05:01.899 --> 00:05:04.899
You look like you have a few pins in the air yourself.

00:05:04.899 --> 00:05:06.899
Just making sure I don't drop any assignments.

00:05:06.899 --> 00:05:19.860
Since we started seeing each other, we never really see each other.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.860
Maybe we should...

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:23.860
Stop and smell the roses.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:28.399
I know where we can find some.

00:05:28.399 --> 00:05:30.399
Across the street, romantic cafe.

00:05:30.399 --> 00:05:34.509
I see a table for two in our...

00:05:34.509 --> 00:05:45.819
Clark. Who's the femme Patel?

00:05:45.819 --> 00:05:49.100
An assignment that I can't put off.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:53.100
Guess we should just hit the pause button on our rosy rendezvous.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:55.100
Thanks. I'm sorry.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:59.279
It's fine. I want to Smallville.

00:05:59.279 --> 00:06:01.279
Got one to Pulitzer.

00:06:01.279 --> 00:06:03.279
I thought we agreed. The daily plan is off-limit.

00:06:03.279 --> 00:06:07.279
I had no choice. I didn't want a risk so I'm finding out that I was contacting you.

00:06:07.279 --> 00:06:09.279
you.

00:06:09.279 --> 00:06:11.279
He doesn't trust you, Calell.

00:06:11.279 --> 00:06:13.279
But I think

00:06:13.279 --> 00:06:15.279
to be the only person that can find my sister.

00:06:15.279 --> 00:06:19.069
Paula?

00:06:19.069 --> 00:06:20.069
She's been kidnapped.

00:06:20.069 --> 00:06:37.980
I'm not judging by the grim look on your face.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.980
I'd say you're not here for the peep show.

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:41.980
Who died?

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:43.980
My billion-dollar dream.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:46.980
For an energy-efficient solar tower.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:48.980
And given what it's cost our company,

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:50.980
I want to know why you're not grieving.

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:52.980
Um, because I think we can come up

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:54.980
with a more fiscally responsible way to

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.980
make the future brighter, greener.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:58.980
Really? Yeah.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.980
Or maybe you're not shedding any tears because you're happy

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.980
that somebody torched that tower.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:04.980
I hope you're not pointing a finger at me

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:08.980
because I think the investigators concluded that it was a freak accident, right?

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:10.980
So it's just a coincidence then?

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:12.980
There was a time

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:15.980
when I could stare into those big brown eyes of yours

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:18.980
and believe anything you told me.

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:24.550
Those days are history.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:30.009
Believe me or not,

00:07:30.009 --> 00:07:32.009
I did what I did because you were bleeding the company dry.

00:07:32.009 --> 00:07:34.009
any dry.

00:07:34.009 --> 00:07:38.009
Well, I'm glad to see that you suddenly care about staying in the black.

00:07:38.009 --> 00:07:39.009
Oh, yeah.

00:07:39.009 --> 00:07:42.009
Because my divisions aren't the only ones wrecking the bottom line.

00:07:42.009 --> 00:07:45.009
I had breakfast this morning with the CFO and he revealed that

00:07:45.009 --> 00:07:48.009
somebody at one of your subsidiaries is embezzling funds.

00:07:48.009 --> 00:07:54.339
So I suggest that you find the money drain.

00:07:54.339 --> 00:07:56.339
Stop the leak.

00:07:56.339 --> 00:08:23.269
You're too late. I'm taking care of this.

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:26.269
I've made sure the police know nothing about it.

00:08:26.269 --> 00:08:28.269
I've cleared up before the owner arrives.

00:08:28.269 --> 00:08:30.649
Why don't you?

00:08:30.649 --> 00:08:32.649
go back to saving humans, Kowel.

00:08:32.649 --> 00:08:33.649
I'm here to find Vala.

00:08:33.649 --> 00:08:35.649
Well, I don't want your help.

00:08:35.649 --> 00:08:39.649
If you hadn't demanded we assimilate, Vala wouldn't be in danger.

00:08:39.649 --> 00:08:41.649
You can't blame me for her abduction.

00:08:41.649 --> 00:08:43.649
You are to blame.

00:08:43.649 --> 00:08:45.649
For sending everyone away from me.

00:08:45.649 --> 00:08:52.399
Now you wanted to drive a wedge between me and my people.

00:08:52.399 --> 00:08:56.399
And now Vala and the others are gone.

00:08:56.399 --> 00:08:57.399
The others?

00:08:57.399 --> 00:08:58.399
Yeah.

00:08:58.399 --> 00:09:02.539
Two other Kandoreans are missing.

00:09:02.539 --> 00:09:04.539
Taken the same way.

00:09:04.539 --> 00:09:05.539
They're crest.

00:09:05.539 --> 00:09:08.539
Left behind is a warning to us all.

00:09:08.539 --> 00:09:21.940
Someone is hunting us.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:24.940
And we can't defend ourselves because you will not give us our powers.

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:27.940
I told you before I can't just give them to you.

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:43.970
And you've made sure to seal our faith by burning down my tower.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:46.970
Police may have written this off as an accident, but you and I both know the truth.

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:52.720
At least have the courage to admit what you've done.

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:54.720
What I did was right.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:55.720
For the humans.

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:56.720
For everyone!

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.720
The Kandorians won't see it that way.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:00.720
You'll never tell them because you don't know which ones have turned against you already.

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:02.720
against you already.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.720
And the fact that that tower is down

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:07.720
leaves you weaker than ever.

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:09.720
Think of me what you will.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:13.720
But know that because of your actions.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:16.720
Our people's blood is on your hands.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:11:00.029
Just let me out, please.

00:11:00.029 --> 00:11:03.029
No, I don't want you contaminating anything, alien.

00:11:03.029 --> 00:11:06.029
I'm not what you think I am. I'm not.

00:11:06.029 --> 00:11:08.029
Oh, I know who you are.

00:11:08.029 --> 00:11:11.029
I thought all of you had vanished off the face of the Earth.

00:11:11.029 --> 00:11:12.029
of the earth.

00:11:12.029 --> 00:11:15.029
But when I spotted you and the others living among us,

00:11:15.029 --> 00:11:17.029
pretending to be humans,

00:11:17.029 --> 00:11:22.029
and realized, you want to colonize our planet.

00:11:22.029 --> 00:11:23.029
No, you're wrong.

00:11:23.029 --> 00:11:24.029
You're wrong.

00:11:24.029 --> 00:11:25.029
You're wrong.

00:11:25.029 --> 00:11:26.029
I'm human.

00:11:26.029 --> 00:11:27.029
I'm the same as you.

00:11:27.029 --> 00:11:28.029
Stop lying.

00:11:28.029 --> 00:11:31.730
I'm gathering in deniable proof.

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:34.730
I'm going to share with the rest of the world.

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.730
And when they learn the truth,

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:41.730
all of you will be hunted down and exterminated.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:12:12.690
Just the interruption I was hoping for.

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:38.080
I like where this is going, Romeo,

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:48.179
but you might want to put on some software music.

00:12:48.179 --> 00:12:51.909
I think Test Muster might be listening.

00:12:51.909 --> 00:12:53.909
She's up to something that involves you.

00:12:53.909 --> 00:12:59.139
She came by my office today.

00:12:59.139 --> 00:13:03.139
With evidence, that someone's been siphoning money from my company.

00:13:03.139 --> 00:13:16.500
You're stealing from me.

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:18.500
A lot of women have used me for my money. I never expected it from you.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.500
I wasn't stealing from you, Oliver.

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:22.500
I was borrowing the cash.

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:27.389
I'm buying insurance for the entire planet.

00:13:27.389 --> 00:13:37.899
Have you found my sister?

00:13:37.899 --> 00:13:38.899
I found my sister?

00:13:38.899 --> 00:13:40.899
Not yet, but I haven't given up.

00:13:40.899 --> 00:13:42.899
Azad told me that three Kandorians were abducted.

00:13:42.899 --> 00:13:46.370
Is that true?

00:13:46.370 --> 00:13:48.370
What was Val's connection to the other two?

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:53.370
They're what you call cybernetic engineers.

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:59.450
Together they were performing tests

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:04.779
to get our powers.

00:14:04.779 --> 00:14:10.100
Perhaps these tests are to blame for her abduction.

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:11.100
You can tell me.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:19.539
They were experimenting on humans.

00:14:19.539 --> 00:14:39.529
You know Noir? For one?

00:14:39.529 --> 00:14:57.710
Miss Lane.

00:14:57.710 --> 00:15:04.710
I'm Dr. Bernard Chisholm. Forgive me for being so forward, but I have a news story I think you should hear.

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:09.710
Sorry, Doc. You just got me on a night when work is the last thing I want to think about.

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:18.889
It'll make your career are living among us.

00:15:18.889 --> 00:15:27.080
Okay. Tell you what, pal.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:31.080
The next time that you want to get a hot tip to a reporter, just...

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:33.080
Try an envelope and a 44-cent stamp.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:40.000
stamp?

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.000
I did.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:44.000
Dozens of times, in fact.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:49.000
While considering your story's alien angle, those letters probably never made it off the wacko pile.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:53.240
I can prove my claims.

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:59.659
I've captured some of them.

00:15:59.659 --> 00:16:02.659
They're under lock and key, had a safe location outside the city.

00:16:02.659 --> 00:16:05.659
Come with me, Miss Lane, I'll show you.

00:16:05.659 --> 00:16:07.659
Help me spread the word.

00:16:07.659 --> 00:16:13.279
Together we'll defend the human race.

00:16:13.279 --> 00:16:15.279
You're very convincing.

00:16:15.279 --> 00:16:17.279
I just need to call my editor.

00:16:17.279 --> 00:16:23.299
Call my editor and let him know that I'm following a hot lead.

00:16:23.299 --> 00:16:24.299
Damn cell phone.

00:16:24.299 --> 00:16:26.299
Never a signal when you need one.

00:16:26.299 --> 00:16:28.299
Just, I'm gonna try out there.

00:16:28.299 --> 00:16:30.299
Just stay here.

00:16:30.299 --> 00:16:32.299
Okay? Don't go anywhere.

00:16:32.299 --> 00:16:48.700
What's your emergency?

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:52.100
Never mind, false alarm.

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:57.500
I'd hope you'd enlist to fight our war.

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:09.549
But I guess you'll have to be drafted.

00:17:09.549 --> 00:17:12.549
This blood confirms my suspicions.

00:17:12.549 --> 00:17:16.549
These things are alien.

00:17:16.549 --> 00:17:20.549
Now, I've kept copious notes about my findings.

00:17:20.549 --> 00:17:26.210
But if I try to share them, they'll be dismissed.

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:28.210
If they come from a legitimate news source,

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.210
the public will listen.

00:17:30.210 --> 00:17:32.210
And that's where you come in.

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:37.210
Listen, Agent Mulder, I will write your X-Files' expose.

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:41.210
But I'm telling you, no one will believe it.

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:47.789
They will when they receive the body parts I've harvested.

00:17:49.549 --> 00:17:52.549
I'm sending samples to medical experts all over the world.

00:17:52.549 --> 00:17:53.549
When they see the proof, they'll come.

00:17:53.549 --> 00:17:54.549
the proof they'll come.

00:17:54.549 --> 00:18:03.819
Cryogenically preserved specimen waiting for them.

00:18:03.819 --> 00:18:10.019
Okay, uh-uh, buddy.

00:18:10.019 --> 00:18:13.019
You just went from creepy critter to full-blown nutjo.

00:18:13.019 --> 00:18:15.019
You need to get that girl out of that Ziploc

00:18:15.019 --> 00:18:17.019
and turn off the deep freeze now.

00:18:17.019 --> 00:18:29.720
You're not appreciating the magnitude of my discovery, Miss Lane.

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:32.720
It's an alien!

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:49.180
Look what they did to me.

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:53.180
Last thing that I remember, I died of a heart attack.

00:18:53.180 --> 00:18:55.180
They brought me back to life.

00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:56.180
They...

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:57.180
They...

00:18:57.180 --> 00:19:03.180
Implanted these into my brain.

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.180
Wait.

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:09.180
You were doing this to her because she saved your life?

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:11.180
You should be thanking her.

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:14.180
Not turning her into a popsicle.

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:16.180
That thing didn't save me.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:27.700
When I died, but then whatever they did,

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:31.700
it's like I can't shut off my brain.

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:33.700
You know, I can't stop thinking.

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:35.700
Thank you.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:38.700
And I have thoughts that a person should never have.

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:43.559
The invasion has begun Miss Lane.

00:19:43.559 --> 00:19:47.559
And it's our job to save mankind.

00:19:47.559 --> 00:19:54.430
The nurse said the medical examiner will be with us any minute.

00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:56.430
How many people are deviling the others work on?

00:19:56.430 --> 00:20:00.430
All I know is they stole the cadavers from the morgue to perform their tests.

00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:03.430
When the test failed, they left the bodies behind for the authorities to find.

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:05.430
They didn't kill anyone.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:07.430
That doesn't make it right.

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:08.430
These people didn't agree to be...

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:10.930
didn't agree to be guinea pigs in your quest for power.

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:12.930
Dead or alive, Zod should never have allowed it.

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:20.180
Zahd didn't know.

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:22.680
Given the way I've seen him command his troops,

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.180
I find that hard to believe.

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:25.680
You've only known the man a few short weeks.

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:27.180
You have no right to pass judgment on him.

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:29.180
Let's just say I know him better than you think.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:30.180
Really?

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:32.180
Were you by his side in the Argo Valley,

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:35.180
where he almost died defending us all?

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:38.180
He ran behind enemy lines alone

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:41.180
to carry a young cadet to safety,

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:43.180
withstood laser scars and shrapnel wounds

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:43.680
to bring her.

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:48.619
back home. That cadet was me.

00:20:48.619 --> 00:20:52.029
And if it wasn't for Zod,

00:20:52.029 --> 00:20:54.029
I wouldn't be alive today.

00:20:54.029 --> 00:20:59.329
He's always been a hero.

00:20:59.329 --> 00:21:02.329
Ready to give his life to protect his people.

00:21:02.329 --> 00:21:04.329
Like the way he protected my father.

00:21:04.329 --> 00:21:07.329
Regardless of their differences,

00:21:07.329 --> 00:21:11.309
be in his heart.

00:21:11.309 --> 00:21:14.309
Zod always consider Joral one of his truest friends.

00:21:14.309 --> 00:21:19.650
I guess it's the sight of Zod I never knew existed.

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:23.650
You may think you have insight into Zod, Kallow.

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:29.960
love. But I assure you, you don't really know the man.

00:21:29.960 --> 00:22:33.940
Pecan Padre.

00:22:33.940 --> 00:22:36.940
What can I do for you, Mugu?

00:22:36.940 --> 00:22:42.940
Well, I have been writing an article on extraterrestrial conspiracy theories.

00:22:42.940 --> 00:22:46.940
People who believe aliens roam the earth, that kind of thing.

00:22:46.940 --> 00:22:51.940
And I've checked with the police, local FBI, and internet groups.

00:22:51.940 --> 00:22:53.940
And I haven't found what I'm looking for yet.

00:22:53.940 --> 00:22:56.940
So, um...

00:22:56.940 --> 00:22:57.940
I figured if...

00:22:57.940 --> 00:23:01.940
If anyone wanted to tell the world, they'd seen little green men,

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:02.940
they might contact us.

00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:04.940
Seems the town's full of your phone nuts.

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:06.940
Be right back.

00:23:06.940 --> 00:23:07.940
Why, thank you?

00:23:07.940 --> 00:24:04.710
Cryptonite weapons.

00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:08.279
This is what you've been spending all of my money on?

00:24:08.279 --> 00:24:10.279
Something that could kill Clark?

00:24:10.279 --> 00:24:12.279
They're to protect all of us, including Clark,

00:24:12.279 --> 00:24:15.279
from Zod and all those other Candorians.

00:24:15.279 --> 00:24:16.279
I don't understand.

00:24:16.279 --> 00:24:20.279
I thought you were helping set them all up with licenses and passports.

00:24:20.279 --> 00:24:23.279
All the IDs I gave Clark have computer tracking chips in them.

00:24:23.279 --> 00:24:27.190
I want to keep an eye on the visitors from them.

00:24:27.190 --> 00:24:30.190
eye on the visitors from another planet.

00:24:30.190 --> 00:24:34.529
Welcome to 1984, the soul of an addition.

00:24:34.529 --> 00:24:37.529
Look, Ali, I'm sorry, okay? But I didn't have a choice.

00:24:37.529 --> 00:24:41.529
Our friend's moral compass has gotten us lost more than once.

00:24:41.529 --> 00:24:45.529
I'm not okay with just sitting back and trusting Clark again.

00:24:45.529 --> 00:25:05.619
Look, Chisholm, if you're trying to freak me out, you've already won the Scream Award.

00:25:05.619 --> 00:25:07.619
There's no need for an encore!

00:25:07.619 --> 00:25:15.240
How did you end up in my nightmare on Psycho Street?

00:25:15.240 --> 00:25:18.240
I'm with the FBI. We've been watching Chisholm for a while.

00:25:18.240 --> 00:25:21.240
She's in for a while. Where are the others?

00:25:21.240 --> 00:25:25.240
There's only one person left alive. She's over there.

00:25:25.240 --> 00:27:02.609
She's must have done to you. Deadline to meet.

00:27:02.609 --> 00:27:04.609
Glad to see that you are, too, G-Man.

00:27:04.609 --> 00:27:13.359
What do you say? We take a look.

00:27:13.359 --> 00:27:14.359
We're just...

00:27:14.359 --> 00:27:18.359
I'm gonna put some pressure on it, and everything will be as good as gold in no time, right?

00:27:18.359 --> 00:27:24.359
Don't worry.

00:27:24.359 --> 00:27:27.359
I won't leave until your FBI backup gets here.

00:27:27.359 --> 00:27:30.799
Why would you do that? You don't know me?

00:27:30.799 --> 00:27:34.069
What Clark would do?

00:27:34.069 --> 00:27:45.900
So you need to help that girl?

00:27:45.900 --> 00:27:49.980
You get out of you.

00:27:49.980 --> 00:27:52.349
You save yourself.

00:27:52.349 --> 00:28:04.089
I don't think I should be talking to reporters about hospital business.

00:28:04.089 --> 00:28:06.089
I need this job.

00:28:06.089 --> 00:28:10.089
Dr. Flores, we already know that the bodies were taken from the morgue last September.

00:28:10.089 --> 00:28:12.089
I just need to know if they were recovered.

00:28:12.089 --> 00:28:15.089
All. Except to...

00:28:15.089 --> 00:28:24.289
This one.

00:28:24.289 --> 00:28:26.289
John Corbin. Now you guys have to go.

00:28:26.289 --> 00:28:28.289
Are there any witnesses?

00:28:28.289 --> 00:28:32.289
Someone who could identify the people responsible for stealing the bodies?

00:28:32.289 --> 00:28:34.289
I have no idea.

00:28:34.289 --> 00:28:35.289
You'd have no idea.

00:28:35.289 --> 00:28:37.289
I have to ask the attending ME who was here at the time.

00:28:37.289 --> 00:28:39.289
When does he get in?

00:28:39.289 --> 00:28:41.289
Dr. Chisholm was forced to take a leave of absence.

00:28:41.289 --> 00:28:43.289
Psychiatric reasons.

00:28:43.289 --> 00:28:46.289
You're gonna have to be more specific than that.

00:28:46.289 --> 00:28:47.289
I've said all I'm gonna say.

00:28:47.289 --> 00:28:50.569
Fine.

00:28:50.569 --> 00:28:52.569
Then I'll have to make up the rest and quote you as the source.

00:28:52.569 --> 00:28:59.670
Because that's what reporters do when they don't have all the details.

00:28:59.670 --> 00:29:01.670
Okay.

00:29:01.670 --> 00:29:04.670
Chisholm said he caught the body snatchers here in the morgue,

00:29:04.670 --> 00:29:06.670
but he was so freaked out by it,

00:29:06.670 --> 00:29:08.670
that he had a heart attack and died.

00:29:08.670 --> 00:29:14.670
Then he claimed that they brought him back to life because they were extraterrestrials.

00:29:14.670 --> 00:29:18.670
Told everybody they experimented on his brain.

00:29:18.670 --> 00:29:23.670
Give me a way to get in touch with him and I promise I won't mention you in the article once.

00:29:23.670 --> 00:29:29.059
Deal.

00:29:29.059 --> 00:29:31.059
Here's contact info.

00:29:31.059 --> 00:29:34.059
But if he's talking to aliens, I doubt he'll want to talk to you.

00:29:34.059 --> 00:29:48.190
Where'd she go?

00:29:48.190 --> 00:30:37.900
Everywhere.

00:30:37.900 --> 00:30:43.380
infiltrated our world.

00:30:43.380 --> 00:30:45.380
But you will not win.

00:30:45.380 --> 00:30:48.380
You don't belong on this planet.

00:30:48.380 --> 00:30:53.730
Your invasion stops now.

00:30:53.730 --> 00:32:46.779
My father's last wish was to save your life.

00:32:46.779 --> 00:32:51.779
Expect from Joe Rowe.

00:32:51.779 --> 00:32:55.579
You don't speak.

00:32:55.579 --> 00:32:57.579
We need to get you a hospital.

00:32:57.579 --> 00:33:20.250
Zod!

00:33:20.250 --> 00:34:47.619
You said they were in there.

00:34:47.619 --> 00:34:49.619
Miss Mercer, I showed you the pictures.

00:34:49.619 --> 00:34:52.619
Those crates were in this container, hundreds of them.

00:34:52.619 --> 00:34:54.619
They're not there now.

00:34:54.619 --> 00:34:56.619
You wanted a higher pay grade, Lenkoff.

00:34:56.619 --> 00:34:58.619
Prove to me you're worth it.

00:34:58.619 --> 00:35:01.619
Whatever they're spending that money on, you find it!

00:35:01.619 --> 00:35:18.760
I figured Tuss was up to something,

00:35:18.760 --> 00:35:21.760
and she gave me the tip about all the money that you, um,

00:35:21.760 --> 00:35:24.760
borrowed, so I moved your stockpile.

00:35:24.760 --> 00:35:28.760
So what other dirty little tricks do you think the amazing Mercer has up her sleeve?

00:35:28.760 --> 00:35:30.760
It's too soon to tell.

00:35:30.760 --> 00:35:34.760
Clark saw a future that we want to run away from.

00:35:34.760 --> 00:35:38.760
You said Tess saw the same future, maybe she wants to take us there.

00:35:38.760 --> 00:35:40.760
Which is why we need those weapons now more than ever.

00:35:40.760 --> 00:35:42.760
more than ever.

00:35:42.760 --> 00:35:44.760
Where'd you put them?

00:35:44.760 --> 00:35:45.760
They're in a safe place.

00:35:45.760 --> 00:35:47.760
Are you keeping me in the dark because I lied to you?

00:35:47.760 --> 00:35:50.760
Well, you know, Chloe, you can't have a set of rules for yourself

00:35:50.760 --> 00:35:52.760
and then a whole other set of rules for everyone else.

00:35:52.760 --> 00:35:54.760
Clark's in the Ken Dorian family now,

00:35:54.760 --> 00:35:58.760
and I don't want to let his loyalties lead us into another doomsday scenario.

00:35:58.760 --> 00:36:00.760
Neither do I.

00:36:00.760 --> 00:36:03.760
So do you really think we should tell Clark everything?

00:36:03.760 --> 00:36:09.469
Absolutely.

00:36:09.469 --> 00:36:21.199
But only when the time is right.

00:36:21.199 --> 00:36:22.199
That, please.

00:36:22.199 --> 00:36:26.849
I need a blood sample analyzed.

00:36:26.849 --> 00:36:27.849
Sample analyzed.

00:36:27.849 --> 00:36:36.860
Lois, what are you doing here?

00:36:36.860 --> 00:36:38.860
The first thing the doctor said when you got released from MetGen

00:36:38.860 --> 00:36:40.860
was to take it easy.

00:36:40.860 --> 00:36:42.860
Their time, Smallville.

00:36:42.860 --> 00:36:46.860
I got Randall to let me pin my Silence of the Lamb's remake.

00:36:46.860 --> 00:36:49.860
The bummer is, the support cast didn't show up to set.

00:36:49.860 --> 00:36:52.860
Our icy ingenue refused treatment at MetGen

00:36:52.860 --> 00:36:54.860
and left no contact info.

00:36:54.860 --> 00:36:55.860
Maybe she wanted to see her own physician.

00:36:55.860 --> 00:36:57.860
What about Zod?

00:36:57.860 --> 00:37:01.860
Both the FBI field office and DC headquarters say they have no record of him.

00:37:01.860 --> 00:37:02.860
Of course.

00:37:02.860 --> 00:37:05.860
It's because Zod works deep cover.

00:37:05.860 --> 00:37:08.860
The FBI would never even admit that he works there.

00:37:08.860 --> 00:37:11.860
It's top secret. That's why I didn't tell you that he was an agent.

00:37:11.860 --> 00:37:12.860
That's the thing about heroes.

00:37:12.860 --> 00:37:14.860
No matter how brightly you shine the light on them,

00:37:14.860 --> 00:37:16.860
they always want to stay in the shadows.

00:37:16.860 --> 00:37:19.860
But still, something doesn't quite add up.

00:37:19.860 --> 00:37:26.239
You're hiding something, Smolville.

00:37:26.239 --> 00:37:29.239
Some other earth-shattering detail about Zod.

00:37:29.239 --> 00:37:31.239
You want full disclosure?

00:37:31.239 --> 00:37:32.239
Great.

00:37:32.239 --> 00:37:33.239
It's a two-way street.

00:37:33.239 --> 00:37:36.239
You're going to have to tell me what you're hiding in your desk drawer.

00:37:36.239 --> 00:37:39.059
Do you should.

00:37:39.059 --> 00:37:45.469
Mr. Kent, why don't we both just agree that a little mystery was good for the romance?

00:37:45.469 --> 00:37:51.530
You first.

00:37:51.530 --> 00:38:04.420
Wellis, I should follow up in an assignment.

00:38:04.420 --> 00:38:07.730
See you on the front page, Jason.

00:38:07.730 --> 00:38:43.260
I trust Lois as well.

00:38:43.260 --> 00:38:47.260
Thanks to you. She told me what happened. You saved her.

00:38:47.260 --> 00:38:56.250
Well, she did a great job of protecting me too.

00:38:56.250 --> 00:39:00.719
I can see why you care for her.

00:39:00.719 --> 00:39:03.719
How are you feeling?

00:39:03.719 --> 00:39:07.480
Like a changed man.

00:39:07.480 --> 00:39:08.480
When your enemy becomes your...

00:39:08.480 --> 00:39:12.480
becomes your saviour, your paradigm shifts.

00:39:12.480 --> 00:39:21.789
Keller, how did you know that your blood would cure me?

00:39:21.789 --> 00:39:25.329
I didn't.

00:39:25.329 --> 00:39:27.329
It must have healed you because you're kryptonian like me.

00:39:27.329 --> 00:39:32.619
You're still in pain?

00:39:32.619 --> 00:39:36.820
Oh.

00:39:36.820 --> 00:39:39.820
Wounds, I was shot, and unlike you, I'm not made of steel.

00:39:39.820 --> 00:39:46.269
You'll be better than new in no time.

00:39:46.269 --> 00:39:49.800
I am better.

00:39:49.800 --> 00:39:54.900
Because I was wrong about you.

00:39:54.900 --> 00:39:58.889
You do care about the Kandori incident.

00:39:58.889 --> 00:40:02.809
And when you saved my life,

00:40:02.809 --> 00:40:09.260
I realized that I can trust you.

00:40:09.260 --> 00:40:12.179
And together we're all.

00:40:12.179 --> 00:40:16.179
We'll make sure that our people can call Earth their new home.

